A||||13||killerb15||Should I Buy This 86 GT?????||||5||
Z||000000||killerb15||11-19-2000||10:26 AM||||Dear Fiero Owners or whoever<P>I'm 15 and wondering if i should purchace a 86 Gt. The owner says the car is in good cond. and runs excellent. Fully Loaded, and it hasn't been in any accidents, all it apparently needs is a vac. line for the brakes. The only problem is that the car has  250,000 highway km's (around 130,000 miles)<BR>Is the car worth the $1000 obo (Canadian) he is asking for it, or should i say forget it??<P>Any help would be appreciated! ||||reg||5
Z||000001||BAM-BAM||11-19-2000||10:51 AM||||   Make sure you take some one with you to look at it who has a good mechanical background. If everything is ok, just say your not sure and offer 900.00 . When he accepts the offer and you  get the car home, begin laughing like a fiend because you just "STOLE" an 86GT.IT seems that maybe this guy has no idea what the car is worth or he's a good friend making you a deal. Either way It's a good deal, IF what he says is true. Let us know.<P> Peace, BAM OUT!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P> P.S. 130,000 miles = under 10,000 a year, not bad.<BR> Peace.<P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT<BR>Eibach/KYB Susp.<BR>Mr.Mikes 500 series seats,headliner! MOMO Commando Steering Wheel, White Face Race Style Gauges And Soon To Be More!!! YEAH BABY-YEAH<p>[This message has been edited by BAM-BAM (edited 11-19-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT Bastard||11-19-2000||10:57 AM||||I'd buy that b*tch with a BLOWN motor for that much money!  Hell yeah...||||reg||1
Z||000003||DavidHenshaw||11-19-2000||11:28 AM||||The answer depends totally on the condition of the car itself. If the interior and exterior are average or better then the car is a "buy" regardless of the engine.  At $1,000 anything you get out of the engine is a bonus. <P>One hundred thirty thousand is not high milage if the engine has been cared for. 50,000 miles is high if its been abused. My 86 GT has 207,000 on its V6, uses very little oil, and will accelerate from 80mph to 100mph very quickly. Thats power. <P>Dave <P>86 GT fastback||||reg||1
Z||000004||killerb15||11-19-2000||03:26 PM||||Thanks all you guys, i'm glad that the car seems to be a good deal and i don't doubt that i can get it for $750(Can.)<P>-I now want to know how reliable the 2.8 is  and how many km's (or miles) its good for?<P>-We had an 86 Camaro with a 2.8 and it had  240,000 km's and the oil was always golden  and ran beautifully, is that the same  2.8 that is in the fiero...<P>-Also is rebuilding the engine in a fiero any  more difficult than most cars?...any more    expencive?...i don't know enough about  engines, or have the tools to do it myself  so i would have to have it rebuilt by a    mechanic...about how much would this  cost  (US Dollars).<P>Thanks In Advance!     ||||reg||10
Z||000005||Tom88gt||11-19-2000||08:48 PM||||Same engine.  Market values of Fieros depend on condition.  The general public has a low image of the car so that keeps prices low.  Look the car over carefully.  If it's in good condition, as compared to other used cars of similar age and mileage, then it's probably a fair deal.  Parts are generally cheap, benefit of being a GM car.  BUT REMEMBER cosmetic, body and trim items are no longer available except in a junkyard.  Deduct heavily for cosmetic flaws.  If the seller didn't fix cosmetic stuff, it's probably because he couldn't find the part, was too cheap to pay for it, or too lazy to find it.<P>But for $1000...any, ANY car that runs and is in good condition is worth at least that.||||reg||1
Z||000006||RiceCooker||11-20-2000||07:42 PM||||I don't think that you should buy it.<P>Send me this guys name, address and phone # and you won't ever have to worry about it again.<P><BR>HAHAHAHAHAHAHAAAAAAAAA  (sinister laugh) ||||reg||1
Z||000007||FieroLisa||11-20-2000||09:07 PM||||Hmmm I'd take the car to a mechanic. That just almost seems too low- $1000 Canadian is like..oh hell, really cheap $US. If you are seriously considering buying it, take it to a mechanic first- it will be worth your money. I bought a car sight-unseen from across the country (Ohio to Louisiana)  with only a mechanic's word. Maybe I just got lucky, but its a great car (86 GT w/ 79 K miles)<BR>And you live in Barrie? My boyfriend goes to school there, Im there at least once a month.<P><P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 gold 4 speed GT<BR>86 gold 5 speed SC (For Sale)<BR>Columbus, OH/Greensboro NC<BR>www.geocities.com/fierolisa/||||reg||12
Z||000008||rockcrawl||11-20-2000||09:50 PM||||Sometimes you just get lucky and find a good deal like that. I saw an ad in the local paper for an '87 GT 98,000 mi. rod knock, but otherwise good condition for $750. Of course I called and went to look at it right away. I was expecting to pull up and see a real beater, but I was pleasantly surprised. It turns out it was a typo and he actually wanted $1500 for it. I took it home for $900 plus a used oscelot exhaust system (for his Formula). It has a nearly flawless interior, a perfectly straight body, alarm, and four new tires. Overall a beautiful car. He said he just needed the money. I think I stole it. I just wish I could find a few more like that. It sounds like you may have found one, I say go buy it!<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||12
Z||000009||kinboyatuwo||11-21-2000||07:48 PM||||If you don't i will <BR>email me an i will pick it up the next day, i have been looking for that kind of deal for a while<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000010||Slammed Fiero||11-22-2000||12:01 PM||||want help in Looking at the Fiero??? I go to Georgian College (In barrie) Fiero lisa is my Girlfriend , if you haven't already made  a decision about buying and want someone to help you look at it , email me @ slammedfiero@excite.com   Lisa will be here Monday we can go take a look at it... I bet you can get it cheaper now ...look at the weather!!. If your looking for a good cheap Fiero I know a few people that can likley help.<P>Jonathan McCreery||||reg||1
Z||000011||killerb15||11-23-2000||04:49 PM||||I Didn't Buy It.....<P>It turns out that the owner was an idiot...<BR>He advertized the car as an 86 GT, the first time i called him he said it was an 86 GT...<BR>Everything seemed fine, and i was ready to go and buy the car on the weekend...even had a trailer lined up that i could use to haul it home on....<BR>I called the idiot...i mean owner to ask him a few small details and after everything seemed fine i was ready to ask him for direstions to get to his house, but i'm was kinda' paranoid about buying my first car so i asked the owner "So the car is definatly an 86, right"...<P>THE OWNER-...Actually...<BR>(nothing good comed after actually...)<BR>The car is an '85...<P>Well i said "thats not the car i'm looking for" and said goodbye.<P>I am still very dissapointed( No-Offence to 85' Owners, their cute but not the car i'm looking for)If anyone knows of an 86-88 gt in Ontario for a reasonable price, or want's info on that '85 GT please leave a message<P>Sincerely <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">iscouraged Teen  ||||reg||9
Z||000012||DavidHenshaw||11-23-2000||05:09 PM||||Don't be discouraged, keep looking.<P>I looked at several Fieros before I found mine. It was advertised for $1900 but I got it for $1500. A white 86 GT fastback with above average original paint and a great looking interior. The V6 had 203,000 miles but had good power and didn't make any smoke. <P>Get a Haynes manual and verify the year model by the serial number. The serial number will tell you a lot about the car. Some of the owners just don't know about the Fiero models. Good luck!<P>Dave||||reg||1
Z||000013||killerb15||11-23-2000||09:05 PM||||Thanks Dave....<BR>   No-matter-what my first car is going to be a Fiero, I'll just have to keep lookin' ||||reg||14
